==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael favorites [options]

List favorites by title.

List favorite areas and projects by title. Archived favorites stay favorites and
are left out unless --include-archived is given; a note under the list says when
any were.

Options:
      --skip <n>
          Number of results to skip. Default: 0.
      --limit <n>
          Page size, 1 to 500. Default: 50.
      --include-archived
          Include archived items.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael favorites
  raphael favorites --limit 20
  raphael favorites --skip 20 --limit 20 --json

Prints:
  One row per item: id, type, state, path, title. JSON carries `items` and
  `page`; paging notes go to stderr.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help output
